[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Zustand: Simple and Scalable State Management in React"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"React applications often require managing state, which can become complex as the application grows. Zustand is a small, fast, and scalable state management solution that simplifies this process. It's un-opinionated and based on simplified flux principles, making it easy to learn and integrate into existing projects."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Why Zustand?"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Simplicity: Minimal boilerplate and easy-to-understand API."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Scalability: Well-suited for both small and large applications."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Performance: Optimized for speed and minimal re-renders."},{"order":7,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Un-opinionated: Works well with various React patterns and architectures."},{"order":8,"type":"bullet_point","text":"TypeScript Friendly: Excellent TypeScript support for type safety."},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"Installation"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"To install Zustand, use npm or yarn:"},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"npm install zustand"},{"order":12,"type":"code","text":"yarn add zustand"},{"order":13,"type":"subheading","text":"Creating a Store"},{"order":14,"type":"paragraph","text":"A Zustand store is created using the `create` function. This function accepts a function that defines the store's initial state and actions."},{"order":15,"type":"code","text":"import { create } from 'zustand';

interface BearState {
  bears: number;
  increase: (by: number) => void;
  decrease: (by: number) => void;
}

const useBearStore = create<BearState>((set) => ({
  bears: 0,
  increase: (by) => set((state) => ({ bears: state.bears + by })), 
  decrease: (by) => set((state) => ({ bears: state.bears - by })), 
}));

export default useBearStore;"},{"order":16,"type":"paragraph","text":"In this example, we define a store with a `bears` state and `increase` and `decrease` actions. The `set` function is used to update the state.  We are also using TypeScript to define the shape of our store."},{"order":17,"type":"subheading","text":"Using the Store in a Component"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"To use the store in a React component, import the `useBearStore` hook and access the state and actions."},{"order":19,"type":"code","text":"import useBearStore from './store';

function MyComponent() {
  const bears = useBearStore((state) => state.bears);
  const increase = useBearStore((state) => state.increase);
  const decrease = useBearStore((state) => state.decrease);

  return (
    <div>
      <p>Number of bears: {bears}</p>
      <button onClick={() => increase(1)}>Increase</button>
      <button onClick={() => decrease(1)}>Decrease</button>
    </div>
  );
}

export default MyComponent;"},{"order":20,"type":"paragraph","text":"Here, we're using the `useBearStore` hook to access the `bears` state and the `increase` and `decrease` actions.  The component will re-render whenever the `bears`, `increase`, or `decrease` values change in the store.  Note that we are subscribing to only the parts of the store that we need.  This is important for performance."},{"order":21,"type":"subheading","text":"Selectors"},{"order":22,"type":"paragraph","text":"Selectors allow you to derive values from the store's state without causing unnecessary re-renders. You can define selectors directly within the `useBearStore` hook."},{"order":23,"type":"code","text":"import { create } from 'zustand';

interface BearState {
  bears: number;
  increase: (by: number) => void;
  decrease: (by: number) => void;
}

const useBearStore = create<BearState>((set) => ({
  bears: 0,
  increase: (by) => set((state) => ({ bears: state.bears + by })), 
  decrease: (by) => set((state) => ({ bears: state.bears - by })), 
}));

const useBearCount = () => useBearStore(state => state.bears);

export { useBearStore, useBearCount };"},{"order":24,"type":"paragraph","text":"Now you can use `useBearCount` in your component, and it will only re-render when the `bears` value changes."},{"order":25,"type":"code","text":"import { useBearCount, useBearStore } from './store';

function MyComponent() {
  const bears = useBearCount();
  const increase = useBearStore((state) => state.increase);
  const decrease = useBearStore((state) => state.decrease);

  return (
    <div>
      <p>Number of bears: {bears}</p>
      <button onClick={() => increase(1)}>Increase</button>
      <button onClick={() => decrease(1)}>Decrease</button>
    </div>
  );
}

export default MyComponent;"},{"order":26,"type":"subheading","text":"Using the `get` function"},{"order":27,"type":"paragraph","text":"Sometimes you need to access the store's state or actions outside of a React component. For this, Zustand provides a `get` function."},{"order":28,"type":"code","text":"import { create } from 'zustand';

interface BearState {
  bears: number;
  increase: (by: number) => void;
  decrease: (by: number) => void;
}

const useBearStore = create<BearState>((set, get) => ({
  bears: 0,
  increase: (by) => set((state) => ({ bears: state.bears + by })), 
  decrease: (by) => set((state) => ({ bears: state.bears - by })), 
  logBears: () => console.log('Current bears:', get().bears)
}));

export default useBearStore;"},{"order":29,"type":"paragraph","text":"In this example, the `logBears` action uses the `get` function to access the current value of `bears` and log it to the console."},{"order":30,"type":"subheading","text":"Middleware"},{"order":31,"type":"paragraph","text":"Zustand supports middleware to enhance the store's functionality. Common middleware includes persist (for saving state to local storage) and immer (for immutable updates)."},{"order":32,"type":"subheading","text":"Persist Middleware"},{"order":33,"type":"paragraph","text":"The `persist` middleware allows you to persist the store's state to local storage or other storage mechanisms. First, install `zustand/middleware`."},{"order":34,"type":"code","text":"npm install zustand/middleware"},{"order":35,"type":"code","text":"import { create } from 'zustand'
import { persist, createJSONStorage } from 'zustand/middleware'

interface BearState {
  bears: number
  increase: (by: number) => void
}

const useBearStore = create<BearState>()(
  persist(
    (set, get) => ({
      bears: 0,
      increase: (by) => set((state) => ({ bears: state.bears + by }))
    }),
    {
      name: 'bear-storage',
      storage: createJSONStorage(() => localStorage),
    }
  )
)

export default useBearStore;"},{"order":36,"type":"paragraph","text":"Now, the `bears` state will be automatically saved to local storage and loaded when the application reloads."},{"order":37,"type":"subheading","text":"Immer Middleware"},{"order":38,"type":"paragraph","text":"The `immer` middleware simplifies immutable state updates by allowing you to mutate the state directly within the `set` function. First, install `immer`."},{"order":39,"type":"code","text":"npm install immer"},{"order":40,"type":"code","text":"import { create } from 'zustand'
import { immer } from 'zustand/middleware'

interface MyState {
  name: string;
  age: number;
  address: { street: string; city: string };
  updateAddress: (newStreet: string, newCity: string) => void;
}

const useMyStore = create<MyState>()(
  immer((set) => ({
    name: 'John Doe',
    age: 30,
    address: { street: '123 Main St', city: 'Anytown' },
    updateAddress: (newStreet, newCity) =>
      set((state) => {
        state.address.street = newStreet;
        state.address.city = newCity;
      }),
  }))
);

export default useMyStore;"},{"order":41,"type":"paragraph","text":"With Immer, you can directly modify the state within the `set` function, and Immer will handle the immutable updates behind the scenes."},{"order":42,"type":"subheading","text":"Conclusion"},{"order":43,"type":"paragraph","text":"Zustand provides a simple, scalable, and performant solution for state management in React applications. Its un-opinionated nature and excellent TypeScript support make it a versatile choice for various projects. By leveraging middleware like persist and immer, you can further enhance the store's functionality and simplify state updates."}]
